      ],
      "text": {
        "hi": "‘a’ मतलब कोई एक: a book = एक किताब। शब्द a, e, i, o, u की आवाज़ से शुरू हो, तो ‘an’: an apple, an egg.",
        "hinglish": "‘a’ matlab koi ek: a book = ek kitaab. Shabd a, e, i, o, u ki awaaz se shuru ho, to ‘an’: an apple, an egg.",
        "en": "‘a’ means any one: a book. If the word starts with an a, e, i, o, u sound, use ‘an’: an apple, an egg."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "learn_card",
      "id": "L3.U05.S02",
      "skills": [
        "grammar.articles"
      ],
      "text": {
        "hi": "‘the’ मतलब ‘वो वाला’, जिसकी बात हो रही है: the sun, the book on the table.",
        "hinglish": "‘the’ matlab ‘woh waala’, jiski baat ho rahi hai: the sun, the book on the table.",
        "en": "‘the’ means one particular thing we both know: the sun, the book on the table."
      }
    },
